# NOTE: dt-blocks.lsp is deliberately NOT ignored.
# It is generated by DT-SETPORT, but it holds the office's measured block
# registry -- names, descriptions and attachment points. Tracking it means a
# new machine gets the calibration along with the code. The cost is that two
# people running DT-SETPORT will conflict on it; if that becomes a nuisance,
# ignore it here and treat measuring as a per-machine step.
# dt-labels.lsp is likewise NOT ignored: generated by DT-SETPREFIX, but it
# holds the office's numbering convention, which should travel with the code.

